WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:03.680
The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System.

00:04.149 --> 00:19.222
It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies.

00:19.730 --> 00:22.534
It is the main source of energy for life on Earth.

00:23.138 --> 00:31.012
The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity.
